INT. SCHOOL GYM - SLEEPOVER - NIGHT

Sleeping bags in a circle. A flashlight in the middle, pointed at the ceiling. Gym mats smell of rubber and old sweat.

ANYA, 15, in pajamas with cartoon cats, sits cross-legged. BARRETT, 16, hugs his knees. DELILAH, 15, plays with the zipper on her sleeping bag. KENJI, 16, sits with a bag of chips he hasn't opened. ROXANNE, 15, stares at the double doors. WALDO, 17, lies on his back, hands behind his head.

ANYA
(to the group)
Okay. Truth or dare. Who's first?

Nobody moves.

BARRETT
(to Anya)
You're the one who wanted to play.

ANYA
I changed my mind.

DELILAH
(to herself)
It's too quiet.

KENJI
It's a gym. Gyms are quiet.

ROXANNE
Not this quiet.

WALDO
There's no wind. No cars. Nothing.

BARRETT
(to Waldo)
Don't say that.

WALDO
I'm just saying.

A basketball rolls out of the dark. Slowly. It bumps against Delilah's sleeping bag. Stops.

Everyone stares at it. Nobody touches it.

KENJI
(whispering)
Did somebody kick that?

ANYA
Nobody's near it.

ROXANNE
(to everyone)
Don't look at the doors.

BARRETT
Why not?

ROXANNE
Because they're open.

They were closed. Now they gape, a black rectangle onto the dark hallway.

Delilah scoots back on her sleeping bag. Kenji drops the chips. Barrett grabs the flashlight and sweeps it across the doors. Nothing. Just the hall.

WALDO
(softly)
Count us.

ANYA
What?

WALDO
Count us. Out loud.

ANYA
One.

BARRETT
Two.

DELILAH
Three.

KENJI
Four.

ROXANNE
Five.

A long pause. Waldo hasn't spoken.

WALDO
Six.

Everyone turns. Waldo is lying exactly as before. But he hasn't moved his lips.

Anya, barely moving her lips, says the only word left.

ANYA
(whispering)
Run.
